  <!-- Harmony dependency added WEAPONS_ABSORPTION_WAVE_1 (2026-08-30): this mod's first
       C# (Source/), porting 7 load-bearing kotorcore comp classes; see items/
       WEAPONS_ABSORPTION_WAVE_1.md. -->
  <!-- kotorcore/VEF/AdaptiveStorageFramework/EBSG/OuterRim Core dependencies added
       ARMOURY_ABSORBED_FRAMEWORK_DEPS_1 (2026-09-02): a minimal-list sweep (BENCH)
       measured that Defs/Absorbed_AdditionalMods/kotorcore/{VEF,AdaptiveStorageFramework,
       EBSG}/*.xml reference those frameworks' own C# classes directly (Class=
       "VEF.AnimalBehaviours...", etc.) with no MayRequire/LoadFolders gate -
       donor kotorcore's own LoadFolders gated this content on framework presence,
       and absorption dropped that gating, making it unconditional. Without the
       framework: SWPotF_RaceDef_ysalamir's whole def is discarded (unresolvable
       Class on a comp), guy762_SecretFloorPanel_BASE's ParentName misses, and
       guy762 implant defs cascade ~60 cross-refs. Separately, RSW_EWebShot's
       damageDef (OuterRim_Blaster) is defined by Outer Rim Core, not shipped here.
       These declarations do not themselves prevent that crash (modDependencies is
       advisory, not a load gate) - they make the requirement visible so
       STARWARS_DONOR_SUNSET_1 or any future donor retirement / reduced mod list
       does not silently break this content. Making the load itself resilient
       (moving these files out of Defs/ into per-framework folders LoadFolders.xml
       can gate) is a larger, separate restructuring - not done here. -->
  <!-- Corrected 2026-08-13, then rebuilt ARMOURY_LOADAFTER_STALE_1 (2026-09-08).
       The 2026-08-13 fix only corrected the two typo'd ids above; it never
       covered the real scope: gen_armoury_patch.py, gen_turret_doctrine.py and
       the hand-authored Armour_*/Warcasket_*/Turrets_*/Flamebow_TagWiden patches
       under Patches/ together emit PatchOperationFindMod/Conditional blocks
       against ~40 third-party (and DLC) mods' ThingDefs, and only 3 packageIds
       were declared. `guy762.kotorweapons` (the old KotOR Weapons donor) is now
       itself DEAD -- that mod was absorbed into this one and retired, so the
       packageId matches nothing installed; it is dropped here in favour of
       `guy762.mm.kotorcore` (the materials mod, still a real donor and already
       below). The full list was built by generating every Patches/*.xml file
       fresh against the live 2026-09-09T01:54:07Z / 590-mod dump (fingerprint
       matches ModsConfig.xml's 590 active mods), collecting every distinct
       <mods><li> FindMod target across ALL patch files (not just the ranged/
       melee ones), and resolving each display name to a packageId off that
       same dump's manifest.json. `Core` (ludeon.rimworld) is omitted: it is
       always first regardless of loadAfter. A loadAfter naming a packageId
       that does not exist, or that is merely inactive, fails/no-ops SILENTLY --
       nothing logs it -- so absent entries are the dangerous failure mode, not
       extra ones; several of these (DLCs, and mods not in every list) are fine
       to declare even when inactive, as an optional-compat statement of intent. -->
